      <description>WAVERLY, Ohio — After years of concern over radioactive contamination in Pike County soil and waterways, newly released testing results show detectable levels of multiple radionuclides in local produce and fish — though health officials say calculated risks remain within federal safety thresholds. The findings were presented as part of an addendum to the Human […]</description>
